PR #755's changed-file coverage gate reported kotlin.py:1027-1073 -- the WI-dorop
enum_entry loop, untouched by that PR -- at 0%. The only test that exercises it,
test_scala_cpp_kotlin_enum_members.py, reaches each analyzer through the registry
(run_analyzer("kotlin", ...)) and imports none of them, so the import-graph slice
never put it in the manifest and CI ran without it. The same blindness holds for
scala.py and cpp.py, whose enum loops the same test covers.

Three lines in .ci/coverage-only-deps.txt (the WI-zaziz mechanism built for exactly
this class) map each of the three analyzers to that test, so smart-test's manifest
augmentation carries it on every future change to any of them. Verified: the
regenerated manifest lists the test and the targeted run reports all changed files
at 100%.

